  "title": "Make Them an Offer They Can\u2019t Refuse ",
  "date": "2025-05-20T16:06:56.895Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n Before you drop a number on a business, learn to think like the original deal pros.\n\n Make Them an Offer They Can\u2019t Refuse\nHi Sara,\nWhen it comes to making offers on a business, you don\u2019t want to come off like a clueless rookie. You want to come in cool, calculated, and compelling.\nSo I created a framework to help you do exactly that. And yes, it\u2019s called M.A.F.I.A.\u2014because who understands business negotiation better than the original entrepreneurs in pinstripes?\nHere\u2019s how to make your offer bulletproof (and maybe a little intimidating\u2014in a good way):\nM \u2013 Market Demand:\nIs it a buyer\u2019s market or a seller\u2019s market? That shiny accounting firm might look unreasonably expensive in May but be 80% of the cost by December. Timing is everything.\nA \u2013 Adjusted EBITDA:\nThis isn\u2019t just about the profit number in the listing. You need to adjust for reality\u2014like whether you\u2019ll be replacing an owner-operator. Because spoiler: hiring someone who knows what they\u2019re doing is not simple and if you do pull it off, it costs money, and that affects your real returns.\nF \u2013 Financing Realities:\nPlease, I beg you\u2014don\u2019t offer a price you can\u2019t actually fund. You need to know if you\u2019re using SBA, cash, seller finance (rare), or investor capital. Pitching a fantasy offer just wastes everyone\u2019s time. Bonus points if you don\u2019t offer terms the bank won\u2019t allow.\nI \u2013 Industry Multiples:\nIf this is the first time you\u2019re hearing \u201cindustry multiple,\u201d stop reading and go Google it. Every industry has them. Don\u2019t offer based on gross revenue unless you want zero leverage when the actual profit numbers look different in diligence. Tie your offer to EBITDA or SDE and show your work.\nA \u2013 Asking Price:\nBuyers often obsess over financials but forget the most important number in the deal: the seller\u2019s real asking price\u2014which has just as much to do with emotions and legacy as dollars. If your offer doesn\u2019t reflect what the seller actually cares about, don\u2019t be surprised when you lose the deal to someone who simply paid more attention.\nFollow these steps, and you\u2019ll go from looking like a hopeful buyer to a serious contender.\nReady to learn how the deal game really works? Check out Deal Academy.\nTo offers that don\u2019t get laughed off the table,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
